 the entire property  belonged to only hair the way that time  travel works in the film is that there's  one set timeline and if you go back and  change things then it affects all future  events and basically wipes things clean  from the moment that they were changed  if someone were to travel back in time  dance on the titanic and steer it out of  the way of the iceberg then when they  returned home their memories of that  being the true history would start to  solidify as if that's the way that it's  always happened this is why adam can  meet his younger self and not remember  it happening to him if he were to return  to 2050 the events i played out would  then become his memories and so on and  so forth hope that makes sense and if it  doesn't yet i'm lost at this point now  you can affect the past which in turn  affects the future and there's several  fixed points in time rather than the mcu  multiverse time split theory this gets  lip service paid to in the film and  hilariously young adam has a childlike  wonder of the equipment and weapons  questioning if one's a lightsaber with  it also being sort of like a tv a time  stick now a big twist comes in the film  when we learn that the timeline we see  is actually one that's already had  somewhat of a deal over and that the  young adam exists in one where saurian  has already gone back and changed a lot  of things we'll talk about this later on  but it's very important to bear in mind  now while saddam initially wants to go  back to 2018 he initially lands four  years later in 2022 he introduces  himself to his younger version who's  played by walker scobel walker is  brilliant in the film and for such a  young guy he does a great job of  recapturing the frantic almost adlib  dialogue that reynolds is famous for you  really can't believe that they're the  same character at different points in  their lives and it helps elevate the  film a lot as they start to work  together now adam's young self is just  as mouthy as he is but he's small and  weak and thus is easily susceptible to  police we find him being tormented by  them leading to him being collected by  his mother and we learn that his father  passed away a year ago which has had a  detrimental effect on him now we get a  pretty cool scene where young adam  realizes just who this man is and elder  adam explains that he's there on a  rescue mission however just as young  adam helps the older one the older one  also helps the young one and it's sort  of like poetry it rhymes in a way now  after the death of his dad adam was very  much like a person who watches the  videos but they don't subscribe they're  there but they're not really there and  because of this he was a complete jerk  to his mother adult adam regrets this  massively as he realizes how nice she  was to him and it's something that he  still loses sleep over it's a poignant  moment and reynolds decides to be the  father figure to his past self that he  lost that one eventually he comes to  realize he might be trying to rush adam  through years of growth and he also  visits his mother at a bar i was really  insisting that they wouldn't do a back  to the future where she'd try and get it  on with him but luckily they dodged that  bullet even if saurian doesn't we're  getting ahead of ourselves but what adam  project is excellently is that it has  these sentimental moments that make it  more than just a time travel story  there's also cool thematic pieces and  even a fight to the song good times bad  times by led zeppelin it's an app choice  and as robert plant talks about losing  his love adam is saved by his wife laura  who sadly doesn't get enough screen time  the song also discusses the idea of what  it's like to be a man and doing the  right thing both of which are things  adam struggles with across time in the  movie along the way adam confronts a  bully who gets some cool hoverboard  riding soldiers and some great action  scenes and also one that's a bit like  the speeder bike chase in return of the  jedi lightsabers and all we also get an  explanation as to what happened to laura  as she's clearly not dead like adam was  told we learned she found something  strange in the jump blocks of a time jet  that returned from 2018. this was never  have supposed to happen and though they  could have just went back to watch  infinity war up at night something fishy  was definitely going on now the real  reason it went there was because saurian  gave tips to her younger self which  changed the time stream meaning it  wasn't the same time that she went to  the past self not only invested heavily  but she managed to gain control of the  time program and she used this for  personal gain even if her head seemed  like it was cgi'd badly onto her body  for the entire movie now sorian going  back in time and changing everything  robbed the entire world of the lives  they were meant to lead and this  included adam it's here that he's urged  to go back to 2018 and end time travel  but in doing this it would mean that  laura and adam never met as they only  cross paths on the programme thus adam  thinks that they needed saurian's  intervention in order to fall in love  and it puts him in a bit of a moral  quandary however laura is adamant that  they're meant to be together and that  their marriage is a sort of fixed point  in time which does get confirmed at the  end of the movie now this moment cuts  even deeper as they're attacked which  leaves laura having to make a final  stand from this point on the two atoms  go back to 2018 this year where they  meet their father played by mark ruffalo  eerily he says most of you will die  before you finish your life's work which  is the exact same thing that happened to  him interestingly they get into a debate  over the origin of the phrase it's  lighter than you think as technically it  is like and then lewis thinks as both  adams are from the future and his story  is lighter than he thinks so lots of  timey tiny whiny wibbly wobbly stuff to  get your head around now lewis despite  being told that the past and future have  already been ruined by saurian refuses  to help put the genie back in the bottle  as he's worried it might further  destabilize the time space continuum  fortunately the theme of young adam  needing a father figure arises again as  old adams says that his younger self  needs him so their mission becomes to  defeat biff tanento saurian now  realizing that he spent too much time on  time travel he decides to go with the  second chance he's been given and thus  the three set out to destroy it once and  for all this all leads to a  confrontation in a super cool fight as  saurian threatens young adam in the  hopes of getting the drive that can  unlock everything while matthew in the  future here it saves the day due to the  metal in the armor-piercing bullets  being magnetic lou is counted on this  and as saurian fires a bullet at him it  gets pulled into the magnetic field of  the generator and thus goes through  saurian's past self in order to continue  its path it's a moment akin to the  ending of looper and because of the  future having to rely on the past  saurian's younger cgidh self dying means  her older version has to die too now  sticking to the rules of how the  space-time continuum should be lewis  refuses to hear how he died sadly it  seems like this is a fixed point in time  and that he was always meant to pass  away no matter what this is confirmed  because we catch a young adam and his  mother at the end of the movie and she's  going through the insurance papers she  says she wants to do what how lewis did  and the whole hug between adam and his  mother doesn't work unless he goes it's  really heartbreaking and watching lewis  accept his fate whilst delivering a  speech about how much he loves his son  really means a lot he trusts in the  strength of adam and knows that no  matter what they are going to make it 30  years takes a long time to correct and  thus they have some time together before  they return to their own times in the  back garden they all play baseball one  last time and ah  i'm not crying you are you are you  stupid punk you're always crying  no young adam promises to give his  mother a hug so hard it could break her  ribs and it's such an emotional ending  about loss acceptance and remembering  the good times amongst the bad watching  them disappear is a great way to say  goodbye and back in the present he  watches young adam tells his mother he  loves her after pretending to mock her  old adam also meets laura and when they  were playing catch he did wonder if  they'd be able to remember the adventure  that they'd gone on as we learned  earlier memories altered to fit the past  however this rule gets broken for the  final few scenes old adam definitely  remembers laura as he said that he found  her and the memories being kept is  further cemented by young adam him  hugging his mother shows he remembers  the final conversation with his older  self and he wouldn't be able to do this  if he'd forgotten everything all in all  it's a really good ending and as for my  thoughts on the movie i had a lot of fun  with it i don't think it's really  inventing the wheel or time travel and  doing anything we haven't seen before  but it still had a lot of dramatic and  great action moments though reynolds is  great and often times he has to carry  movies i think the whole cast here are  really good and zoe saldona mark ruffalo  and walker scobel handle the material  really really well i'm excited to see  what reynolds and levy do next as  they've had two great original ip films  back to back and it's nice to see them  hitting home runs like this on new  properties overall the adam project was  great and it gets an 8 out of 10. i'd  obviously love to hear your thoughts so  make sure you comment below and let me  know if you enjoyed the video then  please hit the thumbs up button and on  screen right now we have a breakdown of  the batman which you should definitely  go check out if not then thanks for  sitting through the video i hope you  enjoy your weekend i'll see you on the  next one you take care peace

